From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] UVM: drain RM-owned non-replayable faults during suspend

The R580 UVM suspend path explicitly leaves the RM-owned non-replayable
fault buffer unflushed. After suspending the top half and flushing its worker
queue, service that buffer synchronously under the same per-GPU service lock
used by the ordinary bottom half. Then flush the kill-channel queue, which
fault servicing may have populated, before returning to RM.

This is a source-level candidate. Runtime PM/fault behavior still requires
validation on a controlled system with the patched module.

--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include "uvm_ats.h"
 #include "uvm_global.h"
 #include "uvm_gpu_replayable_faults.h"
+#include "uvm_gpu_non_replayable_faults.h"
 #include "uvm_mem.h"
 #include "uvm_perf_events.h"
 #include "uvm_processors.h"
@@ -286,11 +287,13 @@
     //     interrupts are handled
     // Due to this, the sequence of suspend operations for each GPU is the
     // following:
-    //   * Flush the fault buffer to prevent fault interrupts when
+    //   * Flush the replayable fault buffer to prevent fault interrupts when
     //     the top-half ISR is suspended
     //   * Suspend access counter processing
     //   * Suspend the top-half ISR
-    //   * Flush relevant kthread queues (bottom half, etc.)
+    //   * Flush the bottom-half queue
+    //   * Service the RM-owned non-replayable fault buffer synchronously
+    //   * Flush the kill-channel queue, which fault servicing may populate
 
     // Some locks acquired by this function, such as pm.lock, are released
     // by uvm_resume(). This is contrary to the lock tracking code's
@@ -317,8 +320,6 @@
         if (gpu->parent->replayable_faults_supported)
             uvm_gpu_fault_buffer_flush(gpu);
 
-        // TODO: Bug 2535118: flush the non-replayable fault buffer
-
         // Stop access counter interrupt processing for the duration of this
         // sleep cycle to defend against potential interrupt storms in
         // the suspend path: if rate limiting is applied to access counter
@@ -331,8 +332,21 @@
 
         nv_kthread_q_flush(&gpu->parent->isr.bottom_half_q);
 
-        if (gpu->parent->isr.non_replayable_faults.handling)
+        if (gpu->parent->isr.non_replayable_faults.handling) {
+            // RM owns the hardware buffer and transfers pending entries to
+            // UVM's shadow buffer on demand. With the top half suspended and
+            // all bottom halves flushed, drain it here so no fault remains
+            // outstanding across the power transition. Use the ISR service
+            // lock because fetch_non_replayable_fault_buffer_entries() and
+            // the normal bottom half require exclusive ownership of the
+            // service state.
+            uvm_parent_gpu_non_replayable_faults_isr_lock(gpu->parent);
+            uvm_parent_gpu_service_non_replayable_fault_buffer(gpu->parent);
+            uvm_parent_gpu_non_replayable_faults_isr_unlock(gpu->parent);
+
+            // Fault servicing can queue an RM channel-kill operation.
             nv_kthread_q_flush(&gpu->parent->isr.kill_channel_q);
+        }
     }
 
     // Acquire each VA space's lock in write mode to lock out VMA open and
